{"name":"Dewberry","hex":"#8b5987","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dewberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in Alberta, Canada.","An unincorporated community in Ripley County, Indiana, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dewberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dewberry","blocks":[{"text":"Dewberries are a group of species in the genus Rubus, section Rubus, closely related to the blackberries. Rubus species referred to as dewberries in North America are small, trailing brambles with aggregate fruits, reminiscent of the raspberry, but are usually purple to black instead of red. In Europe, dewberry primarily refers to Rubus caesius, a plant with arching stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg/330px-Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dewberry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg/500px-P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg/1280px-P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg/500px-P%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rubus caesius","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP%C3%B5ldmuraka_%C3%B5is_Rubus_caesius.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Wild_Dewberries_EAR.jpg/500px-Wild_Dewberries_EAR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail